# Story 2.8. The build context is the raw material of an image, so it carries only what the
# build actually reads: src/ for the API and the core, web/ for the page, and the SDK pin.
# Everything else is either noise in the cache or something that must not be shipped at all.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
_bmad
docs
prototype

# The Dockerfile copies only src/, web/ and the SDK pin, so no test file would be published
# anyway. The rule is wide because tests/fixtures/private holds real GPS traces of real runs
# (AD-9): keeping the tree out of the context altogether means a COPY added later cannot reach
# them even by accident.
tests
tests/fixtures/private

# Build output of the host machine. The image builds its own, and a macOS obj/ would poison
# a Linux restore besides.
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/dist

# Nothing the build reads, and the first two would make every edit to them a cache miss.
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yaml
.env
